+# Performance history
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+Cost of the `SessionStart` health gate on a 5k-record store, p50:
+
+| | p50 |
+|---|---|
+| Before (`quick_check` on the read path) | 11.9 ms |
+| After (`quick_check` off the read path, `fts_rows` counter, `body` CHECK added) | 1.05 ms |
+
+These are measured numbers from an earlier session of this project (tool-observed,
+not a re-derivation or estimate), recorded in
+`~/.local/share/muninn-bench/seed-14a6ab47-frozen.jsonl:22559233`. They were not
+independently re-measured in this session: `cargo build --release -p muninn-cli -p
+muninn-bench` was not run here (the command required approval that wasn't granted),
+so the `muninn-bench perf` tool (`crates/muninn-bench/src/main.rs`, default
+`--records 5000`, reports `SessionStart` hook p50/p95/p99) was not executed to
+corroborate the after-number live. If these figures need to be reverified, run:
+
+```
+cargo build --release -p muninn-cli -p muninn-bench
+target/release/muninn-bench perf --records 5000
+```
+
+The current code already reflects the "after" state: `quick_check` no longer runs
+live on the read path (`crates/muninn-core/src/db.rs::record_quick_check`, cached
+via `meta_get("quick_check_at")`/`meta_get("quick_check_result")` and consulted
+in O(1) by `crates/muninn-core/src/health.rs`), the `fts_rows` counter is read
+from `meta` (`health.rs:294`), and `record.body` carries `CHECK (length(body) <=
+2000)` in `crates/muninn-core/src/schema.sql:16`.
